    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d964">

                <pb facs="0750" n="668" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg668"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé
                            d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-10-26"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 26, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 133.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy
                    and translation of the law<anchor n="1" xml:id="d964-f1"/> enacted by the
                    National Constituent Assembly electing Gen. Luis Mena as President for the
                    constitutional term beginning January 1, 1913, and ending January 31, 1916, and
                    Col. Fernando Solorzano as Vice President for the same period. This law was
                    approved in second debate by a vote of 29 to 2.</p>
                <p>This double elections has been well received. Since it occurred conditions have
                    had a more settled and peaceful appearance than in sometime.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. M. Gunther.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
